    "only_unpenalised_region": "two regions only: (a) m_chi < 3 GeV, where the channel returns 0.0 by the sub-GeV guard, and (b) sigma/m below the switch boundary (~1e-24 cm^2/g at heavy masses), which is many orders below any SIDM regime of interest. In the mass regime the canonical fits actually occupy (400-800 GeV) the channel is at its constant -1.0 penalty for every sigma/m >= 1e-4 cm^2/g, so it adds a constant offset and cannot discriminate between parameter points: it is a flag, not a constraint.",
